## Install

### 1. ROS 2 Jazzy and dependencies

Install ROS 2 Jazzy following the
[official instructions](https://docs.ros.org/en/jazzy/Installation/Ubuntu-Install-Debs.html), then:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install \
  git \
  python3-venv \
  python3-colcon-common-extensions \
  ros-jazzy-desktop \
  ros-jazzy-moveit \
  ros-jazzy-ros2-control \
  ros-jazzy-ros2-controllers
```

Check that ROS is available:

```bash
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
ros2 --help
```

### 2. Clone the simulator

```bash
cd ~
git clone https://github.com/prgrobots/hiwonder_xArm_1s.git
```

### 3. Clone this repository

```bash
cd ~
git clone <https://github.com/agvangavatar/AG_xarm>
cd <AG_xarm>
```

### 4. Python environment

The virtual environment must see the system packages, because `xarm_sim`
uses the `rclpy` that ships with ROS.

```bash
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
python3 -m venv --system-site-packages ~/xarm-sim-venv
source ~/xarm-sim-venv/bin/activate
pip install ~/hiwonder_xArm_1s/xarm_sim
pip install pygame
```

---

## Build

Build the simulator workspace (this repository is plain Python and needs no build step):

```bash
cd ~/hiwonder_xArm_1s
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
colcon build --symlink-install
source install/setup.bash
```

---

## Run

Use two terminals. **Source ROS before activating the virtual environment in every terminal.**

**Terminal A: start the simulator (leave it running)**

```bash
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
source ~/hiwonder_xArm_1s/install/setup.bash
ros2 launch learm_ros2 sim.launch.py
```

RViz opens with the arm. Without a display, add `use_rviz:=false`.

**Terminal B: start the toolkit**

```bash
source /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash
source ~/xarm-sim-venv/bin/activate
cd <path to the folder containing xarm_toolkit>
python run_click.py
```

Click anywhere in the window to aim the arm. Press `Esc` or close the
window to quit.

### Check that the simulator is ready

```bash
ros2 action list            # should include /joint_trajectory_controller/follow_joint_trajectory
ros2 control list_controllers   # both controllers should be "active"
```

### Send a command without Python

```bash
ros2 topic pub --once /xarm/command std_msgs/msg/String \
  "{data: '500/500/500/500/500/500'}"
```

